DESCRIPTION:(1633) Chimay hides a magnitude 11.5 star\, seen from Udaipur.\
 nThe predicted edge passes 37 km to the SSE\, so a miss is likely — but 
 a chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClose
 st approach 23:45:42 IST\, give or take 1 s. The star is 51° up in the SS
 E · dark sky.\nIt fades 4.1 magnitudes for up to 2.6 s on the centre line
 \, and the path is 37 km wide\, give or take 36 km.\nFinder chart\, the ma
 p and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2027-08#2027-08-
 29-1633-chimay-339904
